WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.048
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.318 --> 00:54.284
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

3
01:24.522 --> 01:25.481
It's me.

4
01:33.823 --> 01:35.158
What's going on this late?

5
01:48.838 --> 01:49.797
So he's dead.

6
02:05.146 --> 02:05.980
All right.

7
02:07.565 --> 02:08.608
I see.

8
02:17.367 --> 02:18.326
Wait a moment.

9
02:30.463 --> 02:31.839
You got soaked in the rain.

10
02:43.226 --> 02:44.143
All right, then.

11
02:45.478 --> 02:46.396
Go get some sleep.

12
02:48.398 --> 02:49.607
A castella cake.

13
02:51.776 --> 02:54.070
He told me to buy you that.

14
02:57.240 --> 02:58.074
What?

15
03:00.285 --> 03:02.453
Seo-hee's father…

16
03:05.748 --> 03:07.250
told me…

17
03:09.669 --> 03:12.880
to get you a castella cake.

18
03:16.217 --> 03:19.887
Did I hear that right?

19
03:19.971 --> 03:21.597
On your way home,

20
03:22.807 --> 03:25.393
buy a castella cake.

21
03:27.145 --> 03:28.146
Shut up!

22
03:40.199 --> 03:41.034
That was

23
03:42.327 --> 03:46.497
the last thing he ever said.

24
03:48.833 --> 03:52.712
I didn't know what a castella was.

25
03:59.927 --> 04:04.432
On the day of the March First Movement in Kyeam-ri,

26
04:06.768 --> 04:10.188
Seo-hee had a cold and was unusually fussy that morning.

27
04:12.315 --> 04:13.733
So I asked him

28
04:13.816 --> 04:16.235
if he could stay home that day.

29
04:17.320 --> 04:18.363
Around then,

30
04:19.572 --> 04:21.574
he'd been coming home late every night.

31
04:23.659 --> 04:24.911
But he said

32
04:26.371 --> 04:29.415
he had something important to do and had to go out.

33
04:31.751 --> 04:33.419
Just as he was leaving,

34
04:34.128 --> 04:35.755
he said to me…

35
04:38.800 --> 04:42.095
When spring comes, let's take Seo-hee to Gyeongseong

36
04:43.179 --> 04:44.514
and have some castella.

37
04:45.932 --> 04:47.517
Castella?

38
04:47.600 --> 04:50.144
It's a sweet, soft bread.

39
04:51.396 --> 04:53.398
I'm sure you'll both like it.

40
04:56.692 --> 04:57.735
Sure.

41
05:19.382 --> 05:22.468
Thank you for passing that along.

42
05:47.743 --> 05:49.454
I knew this would happen.

43
07:50.032 --> 07:52.118
-Nieun. -Nieun.

44
07:53.703 --> 07:55.329
-A. -A.

45
07:56.581 --> 07:58.165
-Bieub. -Bieub.

46
07:59.959 --> 08:01.460
-I. -I.

47
08:02.295 --> 08:05.131
-Nabi. -Nabi.

48
08:05.214 --> 08:06.299
A butterfly.

49
08:08.092 --> 08:09.051
Well done.

50
08:09.135 --> 08:10.261
How about we draw one?

51
08:10.344 --> 08:11.637
Yeah, give it a try.

52
09:07.943 --> 09:12.531
HEEWON

53
09:13.699 --> 09:15.993
EPISODE 7

54
09:37.390 --> 09:38.808
Keep an eye on Keum Seo-hee.

55
09:39.308 --> 09:40.643
We don't want any trouble.

56
09:42.895 --> 09:45.523
He should have been given a proper trial.

57
09:47.775 --> 09:48.609
Is he really…

58
09:50.820 --> 09:51.904
with the Gugukdan?

59
09:56.075 --> 09:58.202
You never used to ask questions like that.

60
09:58.285 --> 09:59.120
Why?

61
09:59.787 --> 10:01.914
Have you had a change of heart since coming to Joseon?

62
10:04.375 --> 10:05.918
I told you not to show it, didn't I?

63
10:06.669 --> 10:08.045
Even with me,

64
10:09.088 --> 10:10.673
do not let it show.

65
10:14.969 --> 10:16.470
And yet look at you now.

66
10:18.431 --> 10:20.266
You look like a pathetic little kid.

67
10:34.739 --> 10:41.162
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

68
10:52.465 --> 10:53.549
Thank you.

69
10:59.972 --> 11:00.806
Good morning!

70
11:00.890 --> 11:01.807
Inspector General!

71
11:04.143 --> 11:05.519
-Good morning! -Good morning!

72
11:11.984 --> 11:13.277
-Good morning! -Good morning!

73
11:39.178 --> 11:40.346
The inspector general

74
11:41.388 --> 11:43.182
usually takes the elevator.

75
11:43.933 --> 11:45.643
So you won't run into him often.

76
12:15.589 --> 12:17.466
My mother was a Joseon person.

77
12:23.138 --> 12:24.348
I mean my stepmother.

78
12:25.933 --> 12:28.894
Or I suppose I should call her my adoptive mother.

79
12:30.020 --> 12:32.022
I don't remember my birth mother.

80
12:33.482 --> 12:36.235
My father took me in as his son,

81
12:37.361 --> 12:38.529
and then married her.

82
12:40.447 --> 12:42.324
Apparently, even more so than today,

83
12:42.408 --> 12:44.577
marriages between Japanese and Joseon people

84
12:44.660 --> 12:46.161
were encouraged back then.

85
12:49.081 --> 12:49.915
Right.

86
12:51.292 --> 12:52.668
I know that.

87
12:55.296 --> 12:57.298
We only lived together for a short time.

88
13:01.218 --> 13:03.679
But my mother taught me what love was.

89
13:39.423 --> 13:40.883
She even taught me

90
13:42.092 --> 13:44.595
how it would feel to be abandoned by that love.

91
13:57.858 --> 13:59.109
Mother.

92
14:11.205 --> 14:12.331
Your mother…

93
14:14.083 --> 14:15.376
is not coming back.

94
14:20.214 --> 14:21.340
My mother

95
14:22.049 --> 14:24.176
left us out of the blue one day.

96
14:51.954 --> 14:55.916
Why are you telling me all this?

97
15:04.508 --> 15:05.884
I wanted to apologize

98
15:07.011 --> 15:08.303
for the things I said yesterday.

99
15:09.763 --> 15:11.765
People like you make me sick.

100
15:12.599 --> 15:14.935
People who throw words around…

101
15:15.978 --> 15:17.521
with no intention of standing by them.

102
15:22.151 --> 15:23.110
I'm sorry

103
15:24.778 --> 15:26.113
for what I said yesterday.

104
15:40.919 --> 15:42.087
My mother…

105
15:44.256 --> 15:45.716
abandoned me too.

106
15:47.885 --> 15:49.261
She married a Japanese man.

107
15:50.929 --> 15:51.847
And then,

108
15:53.474 --> 15:54.850
she died.

109
16:01.440 --> 16:03.650
But I'm not someone to pity.

110
16:04.193 --> 16:05.903
I've felt that way a few times,

111
16:07.029 --> 16:09.031
but really, I was just unlucky.

112
16:11.408 --> 16:12.409
The only thing is…

113
16:14.495 --> 16:18.248
if she was going to leave me anyway,

114
16:19.958 --> 16:23.504
I only hope she was happy with him until the very end.

115
16:26.006 --> 16:29.134
Whatever you do, you should at least make sure it was worth it.

116
16:33.764 --> 16:37.851
Anyway, after that, I did my best to get by on my own.

117
16:39.269 --> 16:41.730
Well, I'd say I'm doing pretty well, aren't I?

118
16:42.940 --> 16:46.026
I was cast out onto the streets of Jongno without so much as a worn-out spoon,

119
16:46.110 --> 16:49.071
but I made it out alive.

120
16:55.410 --> 16:56.829
Ms. Keum,

121
16:59.665 --> 17:00.958
you're a good person.

122
17:04.128 --> 17:05.921
That's why it's hard to understand.

123
17:07.923 --> 17:08.799
He…

124
17:11.009 --> 17:12.344
is a married man.

125
17:14.930 --> 17:16.932
You said enough about that yesterday.

126
17:17.015 --> 17:18.851
Did it have to be him?

127
17:24.731 --> 17:27.317
I don't need you to understand me.

128
17:29.278 --> 17:31.405
I'll stop by the post office.

129
17:53.719 --> 17:57.306
I really hate pretending to have an affair.

130
18:11.904 --> 18:12.905
I'm off.

131
18:16.992 --> 18:18.327
I need to ask you a favor.

132
18:20.829 --> 18:21.872
It's about Seo-hee.

133
18:24.249 --> 18:26.293
Please find a way to get her to America.

134
18:27.961 --> 18:29.379
-So-ran. -I know.

135
18:29.880 --> 18:33.592
The United States doesn't allow Asian immigrants right now.

136
18:33.675 --> 18:36.470
Some Joseon people manage to study there,

137
18:36.553 --> 18:38.597
but she never even went to school.

138
18:39.097 --> 18:41.099
And the Government-General already knows about her,

139
18:41.183 --> 18:43.810
so forging her paperwork for studying abroad wouldn't be easy.

140
18:43.894 --> 18:48.398
Yes, that's why we planned to pay her off and settle things once this was over.

141
18:48.482 --> 18:50.525
I feel bad for lying about sending her to America,

142
18:50.609 --> 18:51.985
but she does love money--

143
18:52.069 --> 18:53.445
Yes, that was the plan.

144
18:53.528 --> 18:55.822
We also said that if she turned against us,

145
18:55.906 --> 18:59.660
her very existence could put us in danger.

146
19:01.995 --> 19:05.249
Still, I want to keep her alive and get her to America.

147
19:05.958 --> 19:07.459
I want to keep my promise.

148
19:09.920 --> 19:10.796
Do you mean that?

149
19:11.672 --> 19:12.506
Yes.

150
19:13.590 --> 19:15.968
I believe you'll find a way.

151
19:17.636 --> 19:18.804
Please, I'm asking you.

152
19:33.318 --> 19:35.529
SATO, DIVISION OF REGIONAL AFFAIRS

153
19:37.614 --> 19:39.074
Excuse me.

154
19:39.157 --> 19:42.619
This was put in our mailbox by mistake. It's not for the Foreign Affairs Division.

155
19:44.413 --> 19:45.872
Mr. Sato of Regional Affairs!

156
19:45.956 --> 19:48.625
I saw "Sato" and put it in Foreign Affairs by mistake.

157
19:48.709 --> 19:49.793
Thank you very much.

158
19:49.876 --> 19:53.672
Sato is a common surname, and there are several of them at the Government-General.

159
19:55.757 --> 19:56.758
INSPECTOR GENERAL

160
20:00.095 --> 20:02.139
Suwon Police Station?

161
20:02.889 --> 20:04.766
PERSONAL, CONFIDENTIAL FOR THE ADDRESSEE ONLY

162
20:04.850 --> 20:08.645
TO SATO SHINICHI, THE INSPECTOR GENERAL

163
20:08.729 --> 20:12.232
What could be personal and confidential for the inspector general?

164
20:12.316 --> 20:13.692
His name is Keum Seok-jung.

165
20:13.775 --> 20:15.777
He's from Kyeam-ri, Suwon.

166
20:16.778 --> 20:18.363
Could it be about Kyeam-ri?

167
20:18.447 --> 20:19.448
Kobayashi!

168
20:19.531 --> 20:20.365
Yes, sir!

169
20:30.959 --> 20:31.918
Darn it.

170
20:44.389 --> 20:48.310
Put me through to Inspector Matsui Kenji at Suwon Police Station in Gyeonggi.

171
20:53.482 --> 20:54.858
Yes, Matsui speaking.

172
20:56.443 --> 20:58.528
I'm sorry to interrupt.

173
20:58.612 --> 21:01.198
I'm Sato from Regional Affairs at the Government-General.

174
21:02.240 --> 21:05.744
The reason I'm calling is that I received some mail you sent.

175
21:05.827 --> 21:08.413
I checked the contents, and I don't think it was meant for me.

176
21:08.497 --> 21:09.331
Sorry?

177
21:10.123 --> 21:12.876
I sent that to the Inspector General's Office.

178
21:12.959 --> 21:14.252
How did it end up there?

179
21:15.128 --> 21:15.962
Wait.

180
21:16.546 --> 21:18.382
Then, did you open the envelope?

181
21:18.965 --> 21:22.302
Yes, it was addressed to Mr. Sato at the Government-General.

182
21:22.386 --> 21:24.137
The post office delivered it to me.

183
21:24.221 --> 21:25.931
My goodness, what was I thinking?

184
21:26.473 --> 21:29.935
I guess it wasn't marked as "personal" and "confidential" for the inspector general.

185
21:30.018 --> 21:31.061
No.

186
21:31.144 --> 21:32.896
I can't believe this.

187
21:33.730 --> 21:34.564
I'm sorry.

188
21:34.648 --> 21:36.733
I ended up taking out what was inside.

189
21:36.817 --> 21:39.194
If you give me a list of the documents you sent,

190
21:39.277 --> 21:42.864
I'll put everything in a new envelope and send it to the Inspector General's Office.

191
21:42.948 --> 21:44.991
I'd really appreciate that.

192
21:46.868 --> 21:48.203
The documents I sent were…

193
21:51.581 --> 21:54.584
the report file on the Kyeam-ri riot in 1919,

194
21:54.668 --> 21:58.296
the files on four of the main suspects who were persons of interest,

195
21:58.380 --> 22:00.257
their individual persons of interest cards,

196
22:00.340 --> 22:02.217
along with their court rulings, prison records,

197
22:03.468 --> 22:04.719
and surveillance report.

198
22:05.846 --> 22:08.140
Yes, it's all here.

199
22:08.223 --> 22:10.851
I'll put everything back in place and deliver it. Don't worry.

200
22:10.934 --> 22:13.895
And I'll make sure to mark it "personal" and "confidential" as well.

201
22:15.021 --> 22:16.106
Thank you so much.

202
22:16.189 --> 22:17.065
All right, then.

203
22:17.149 --> 22:18.358
Oh, wait a moment.

204
22:19.192 --> 22:22.279
There should be a family photo in there too.

205
22:24.030 --> 22:25.657
A family photo?

206
22:25.740 --> 22:26.658
Yes.

207
22:26.741 --> 22:29.953
There's a photo of a man named Keum Seok-jung,

208
22:30.036 --> 22:32.205
one of the main suspects, with his wife and child.

209
22:35.625 --> 22:37.043
Yes, I've got it right here.

210
22:37.127 --> 22:38.503
Take care, then.

211
22:38.587 --> 22:39.671
Thank you.

212
22:53.310 --> 22:54.519
Hello there!

213
22:55.228 --> 22:56.521
Hello.

214
22:59.316 --> 23:01.610
You must be Ms. Yamada, the inspector general's secretary.

215
23:02.652 --> 23:03.487
Yes.

216
23:07.699 --> 23:09.159
I'm sorry.

217
23:09.242 --> 23:11.536
I must've surprised you, acting like we knew each other.

218
23:12.204 --> 23:13.038
Sorry?

219
23:14.873 --> 23:18.001
I've heard so much about you from Interpreter Sato.

220
23:18.084 --> 23:20.212
I felt like I already knew you.

221
23:20.795 --> 23:23.548
I'm sorry if I came on too strong.

222
23:25.967 --> 23:28.011
He's been talking about me?

223
23:28.094 --> 23:29.179
Yes.

224
23:29.262 --> 23:31.848
You wouldn't believe how often he talks about you.

225
23:33.058 --> 23:36.228
Just the other day, while eating the cookies you brought,

226
23:36.311 --> 23:38.063
he said, "Ms. Yamada… Ms. Ya…

227
23:41.066 --> 23:43.151
mada is…"

228
23:44.110 --> 23:45.445
Ms. Yamada what?

229
23:46.279 --> 23:47.113
Yama…

230
23:50.075 --> 23:51.535
I'm sorry.

231
23:52.327 --> 23:53.995
It was on the tip of my tongue.

232
23:54.079 --> 23:57.040
I've been so tired lately, so I'm forgetful.

233
23:59.334 --> 24:00.877
I should eat something sweet.

234
24:01.461 --> 24:04.130
That'll help me remember…

235
24:04.214 --> 24:05.048
By any chance,

236
24:06.841 --> 24:08.343
do you like chocolate?

237
24:10.845 --> 24:11.680
Yes.

238
24:12.514 --> 24:15.225
Ms. Wada from our secretary's office is out sick today,

239
24:15.308 --> 24:18.645
so I've been swamped by myself.

240
24:18.728 --> 24:21.773
I didn't even have time to pick up the mail.

241
24:21.856 --> 24:24.818
I just managed to come down after serving tea to the guests.

242
24:26.027 --> 24:27.404
That's quite a lot of mail.

243
24:27.487 --> 24:28.613
Do you want me to help you?

244
24:28.697 --> 24:30.323
No, I'm fine.

245
24:30.407 --> 24:31.575
Oh, right. You're fine.

246
24:33.368 --> 24:34.703
INSPECTOR GENERAL'S OFFICE

247
24:34.786 --> 24:36.830
We have guests inside, so keep your voice down.

248
25:03.023 --> 25:03.857
Come in.

249
25:05.483 --> 25:06.359
Thanks.

250
25:16.995 --> 25:19.414
The new-season catalog is here.

251
25:20.665 --> 25:23.543
This one's for the inspector general…

252
25:26.338 --> 25:28.465
The chocolate is in the break room.

253
25:28.548 --> 25:30.508
One moment.

254
25:30.592 --> 25:32.552
Sure. Take your time.

255
25:32.636 --> 25:33.970
Okay.

256
25:41.061 --> 25:41.936
SUWON POLICE STATION

257
25:42.854 --> 25:44.022
GINZA BOUTIQUE

258
25:52.572 --> 25:53.615
Here you go.

259
25:53.698 --> 25:55.659
Here's chocolate.

260
25:55.742 --> 25:57.035
Thank you.

261
26:01.998 --> 26:04.918
What did Interpreter Sato say about me?

262
26:10.131 --> 26:11.257
He said…

263
26:14.177 --> 26:15.095
Ms. Yamada.

264
26:15.178 --> 26:18.390
I see you have your clothes tailored at Ginza Boutique on Bonjeong Avenue.

265
26:18.473 --> 26:19.683
That's right.

266
26:20.600 --> 26:22.811
This outfit is from there.

267
26:23.561 --> 26:26.022
Of course. I was thinking how pretty it was.

268
26:28.191 --> 26:31.611
Though, of course, you look pretty in anything.

269
26:33.154 --> 26:34.948
I get that a lot.

270
26:36.658 --> 26:39.119
I'll have to go there myself when they get new styles in.

271
26:40.787 --> 26:42.831
This is their new-season catalog.

272
26:42.914 --> 26:43.832
Really?

273
26:44.332 --> 26:46.710
Great! Let's have a look together.

274
26:46.793 --> 26:47.961
Sounds good!

275
26:51.423 --> 26:53.842
Where's the letter opener?

276
26:53.925 --> 26:54.884
What?

277
26:58.555 --> 27:00.765
I can't wait to see the new styles.

278
27:00.849 --> 27:01.766
Found it.

279
27:04.436 --> 27:08.189
When you go to Ginza Boutique, ask for Mr. Hashimoto, not Mr. Kim.

280
27:09.149 --> 27:13.111
Mr. Kim can be awfully frustrating. He never seems to understand.

281
27:13.194 --> 27:15.905
Joseon people are a little slow, you know.

282
27:17.323 --> 27:18.491
No offense.

283
27:19.075 --> 27:20.660
No worries. None taken.

284
27:28.334 --> 27:29.252
Oh no.

285
27:30.128 --> 27:31.129
What's wrong?

286
27:31.713 --> 27:35.592
It's confidential mail meant for the inspector general to open,

287
27:36.259 --> 27:37.635
but I opened it by mistake.

288
27:39.387 --> 27:40.346
What do I do?

289
27:41.389 --> 27:43.641
I mixed up these two envelopes.

290
27:44.768 --> 27:45.643
Oh no.

291
27:45.727 --> 27:46.895
Oh no.

292
27:53.026 --> 27:53.985
Myung-nam.

293
27:54.068 --> 27:55.445
I'm so sorry.

294
28:00.283 --> 28:01.618
Thank you.

295
28:01.701 --> 28:06.206
Oh dear. It seems my daughter was a bit taken aback by the talk of marriage.

296
28:07.582 --> 28:09.209
The truth is,

297
28:09.292 --> 28:12.545
I lured her here by promising tonkatsu on Bonjeong Avenue.

298
28:13.963 --> 28:16.758
I called Hideo here without telling him what this was about, either.

299
28:16.841 --> 28:18.009
Oh dear.

300
28:20.887 --> 28:24.390
This feels like the first chapter of a popular fiction.

301
28:29.187 --> 28:30.021
Goodness.

302
28:31.439 --> 28:32.774
Oh my.

303
28:34.734 --> 28:35.568
Yamada!

304
28:37.779 --> 28:39.948
Did he just call me?

305
28:40.031 --> 28:40.907
Yes.

306
28:42.367 --> 28:43.785
What am I going to do?

307
28:44.869 --> 28:48.373
I'll sort this out. You'd better go on inside.

308
28:48.456 --> 28:50.750
-So he won't get angrier later. -Okay.

309
28:54.921 --> 28:55.922
You got this.

310
28:57.298 --> 28:58.132
Thank you.

311
29:05.598 --> 29:07.225
Did you call for me?

312
29:24.450 --> 29:26.119
1919 THE KYEAM-RI RIOT

313
29:26.202 --> 29:28.204
OFFICIAL CASUALTY LIST

314
29:30.164 --> 29:31.708
Keum Seo-hee…

315
29:35.545 --> 29:36.588
Keum Seo-hee…

316
29:36.671 --> 29:38.423
Not here.

317
29:40.174 --> 29:41.301
Ms. Keum?

318
29:44.095 --> 29:45.555
Why are you here?

319
29:48.725 --> 29:49.684
Mr. Sato.

320
29:52.061 --> 29:53.730
Were you in there?

321
29:53.813 --> 29:54.647
Yes.

322
29:55.315 --> 29:56.524
What are you doing here?

323
29:57.942 --> 30:00.361
I'm running a quick errand.

324
30:00.862 --> 30:02.614
A quick errand?

325
30:02.697 --> 30:05.033
Yes, but I'm done now.

326
30:06.910 --> 30:07.827
Hold on.

327
30:10.038 --> 30:10.914
Stay right there.

328
30:11.664 --> 30:13.166
Your hand behind your back.

329
30:20.173 --> 30:21.424
What is that…

330
30:24.802 --> 30:26.054
in your hand?

331
30:30.058 --> 30:30.934
Can you

332
30:32.644 --> 30:33.728
show me your hand?

333
31:01.506 --> 31:04.550
Well, I gave her that chocolate.

334
31:05.718 --> 31:08.221
Please don't tell the inspector general.

335
31:08.304 --> 31:09.806
I'm asking you, please.

336
31:20.984 --> 31:24.153
I really appreciate you taking the time today.

337
31:25.113 --> 31:27.365
-Well then. -Yes, I'll be in touch.

338
31:27.448 --> 31:28.700
-I'll see you again. -Of course.

339
31:34.205 --> 31:35.248
Hideo.

340
31:35.331 --> 31:36.916
Show Mr. Kim out.

341
31:38.167 --> 31:39.002
Yes, sir.

342
31:39.085 --> 31:40.878
All right, Myung-nam. Say goodbye.

343
31:42.672 --> 31:43.506
Goodbye.

344
31:43.589 --> 31:45.425
We'll be on our way, then.

345
31:45.508 --> 31:46.801
Take care.

346
31:47.593 --> 31:48.428
Let's go.

347
31:55.268 --> 31:56.728
Aren't you going to clean the table?

348
31:58.062 --> 31:59.063
Right away, sir.

349
31:59.647 --> 32:01.649
Is there any new mail?

350
32:02.650 --> 32:03.860
Yes,

351
32:03.943 --> 32:05.069
there is.

352
32:18.916 --> 32:20.460
I'm sorry.

353
32:20.543 --> 32:24.547
I thought it was addressed to me and opened it by accident!

354
32:24.630 --> 32:26.049
Please forgive me.

355
32:31.304 --> 32:32.638
Did you take out what was inside?

356
32:33.765 --> 32:35.475
I only opened it. I swear I never looked.

357
32:35.558 --> 32:37.143
You opened the envelope,

358
32:38.978 --> 32:40.354
but you didn't look inside?

359
32:40.438 --> 32:41.647
I swear.

360
32:41.731 --> 32:42.857
I never looked.

361
32:43.775 --> 32:45.443
I'm terribly sorry.

362
32:53.743 --> 32:56.037
NA BYEONG-SUN

363
32:56.120 --> 32:58.706
KEUM SEOK-JUNG

364
33:38.121 --> 33:39.664
Sorry, madam.

365
33:40.832 --> 33:42.834
It seemed like you didn't have a photo of Seo-hee.

366
33:45.753 --> 33:48.673
I never had a picture of my mom,

367
33:49.757 --> 33:52.093
so I can barely remember her face.

368
34:11.279 --> 34:12.738
When did I get this?

369
34:13.948 --> 34:17.535
Thanks for walking us out. See you soon.

370
34:17.618 --> 34:18.452
All right.

371
34:19.871 --> 34:20.705
Go on.

372
34:40.016 --> 34:41.100
Inspector Matsui.

373
34:41.767 --> 34:43.644
This is Sato, the Inspector General.

374
34:44.478 --> 34:47.106
I want the full list of the materials you sent over.

375
34:59.952 --> 35:01.454
A family photo?

376
35:04.290 --> 35:05.583
Inspector General.

377
35:05.666 --> 35:07.084
It's Interpreter Sato.

378
35:07.168 --> 35:09.170
I see. That'll be all.

379
35:32.485 --> 35:33.319
Help yourself.

380
35:34.654 --> 35:35.655
No, thank you.

381
35:39.700 --> 35:40.910
That was out of nowhere.

382
35:41.619 --> 35:42.536
A marriage?

383
35:44.080 --> 35:46.958
The wedding will be held once the League of Nations Commission

384
35:47.041 --> 35:48.918
finishes their visit to Keijo this summer.

385
35:50.127 --> 35:53.422
Mr. Kim plans to hand Joil Textile Factory over to you within three years.

386
35:53.506 --> 35:55.675
Once you're married, move over to Joil Textile Factory.

387
35:56.175 --> 35:58.177
What good is sitting around as an interpreter?

388
35:58.261 --> 36:00.471
You're only wasting your time.

389
36:00.554 --> 36:03.891
Is this about what's best for me?

390
36:05.017 --> 36:06.185
Isn't it for yourself?

391
36:06.269 --> 36:08.104
Don't be so cynical.

392
36:10.273 --> 36:12.900
A marriage like this is only natural for someone in your position.

393
36:13.401 --> 36:15.403
We each have something the other needs.

394
36:15.486 --> 36:17.321
We exchange what's needed.

395
36:19.657 --> 36:23.536
Surely your marriage wasn't based on a bargain like that.

396
36:25.371 --> 36:26.205
That's right.

397
36:27.665 --> 36:29.500
And I paid a heavy price for that.

398
36:36.007 --> 36:37.591
After that failure,

399
36:38.426 --> 36:42.179
I chose my next marriage based on what I needed and what I hoped to achieve.

400
36:42.888 --> 36:44.849
That's how I came to where I am today.

401
36:47.101 --> 36:48.019
I have no regrets.

402
36:52.898 --> 36:54.066
I guess you regret

403
36:55.693 --> 36:56.819
marrying Mother, then.

404
36:58.154 --> 36:58.988
No.

405
36:59.780 --> 37:01.782
It was a failure, but I don't regret it.

406
37:01.866 --> 37:04.035
I've never regretted my choices.

407
37:06.162 --> 37:07.747
Even if I could turn back time,

408
37:08.497 --> 37:10.124
I'd make the same choice.

409
37:12.001 --> 37:14.337
The same goes for making you my son, Hideo.

410
37:20.092 --> 37:21.052
You hurt your hand.

411
37:23.012 --> 37:24.138
You should be more careful.

412
37:26.849 --> 37:28.225
Just as I have no regrets,

413
37:31.729 --> 37:33.147
I hope you won't either.

414
37:49.455 --> 37:51.499
Why were you at the Government-General?

415
37:52.249 --> 37:54.335
Father wants me to marry the inspector general's son.

416
37:56.879 --> 37:57.755
You startled me.

417
37:59.215 --> 38:01.217
I'm sorry, there was a puppy on the road…

418
38:06.639 --> 38:08.349
By the way, what did you just say?

419
38:09.975 --> 38:10.935
You're getting married?

420
38:12.019 --> 38:13.854
Yes, I am.

421
38:25.783 --> 38:27.159
SUWON POLICE STATION

422
38:27.243 --> 38:29.829
Are these from Suwon Police Station?

423
38:30.538 --> 38:32.790
There's nothing out of the ordinary.

424
38:36.001 --> 38:37.837
Keum Seok-jung is dead.

425
38:37.920 --> 38:39.505
His daughter died back then.

426
38:40.798 --> 38:42.341
Find out where his wife is.

427
38:42.425 --> 38:44.301
If she's dead, find out when and how she died.

428
38:45.594 --> 38:46.429
Yes, sir.

429
38:49.890 --> 38:51.809
So about Keum Seok-jung's interrogation…

430
38:55.271 --> 38:56.105
Yes?

431
38:56.188 --> 38:59.358
He asked specifically for Keum Seo-hee to interpret.

432
39:00.776 --> 39:01.610
Yes, he did.

433
39:05.030 --> 39:07.992
Look into Keum Seo-hee's record. Her past, all of it. Leave nothing out.

434
39:09.368 --> 39:10.202
Yes, sir!

435
39:14.248 --> 39:15.541
RELIEF FOR KIDS' CONSTIPATION

436
39:15.624 --> 39:16.667
Kkot-nim.

437
39:17.501 --> 39:19.295
Why aren't you taking that?

438
39:19.378 --> 39:22.256
Ga-kyung gave this to me.

439
39:23.132 --> 39:24.341
I want to save it.

440
39:25.092 --> 39:26.093
Don't be silly.

441
39:26.177 --> 39:27.678
Medicine is meant to be taken.

442
39:28.471 --> 39:29.388
Use it or lose it.

443
39:29.472 --> 39:30.431
Geum-ok.

444
39:31.015 --> 39:31.891
Hey, Mr. Lee!

445
39:31.974 --> 39:33.767
Hello.

446
39:33.851 --> 39:34.935
Kkot-nim is here too.

447
39:35.811 --> 39:36.645
Perfect.

448
39:39.356 --> 39:40.316
Have some potatoes.

449
39:40.399 --> 39:41.400
Oh my.

450
39:43.277 --> 39:45.237
Goodness, thank you.

451
39:45.321 --> 39:47.281
Wow, thank you.

452
39:47.364 --> 39:48.824
Where'd you get the potatoes?

453
39:49.408 --> 39:50.826
Did you go haul a load?

454
39:50.910 --> 39:51.785
Yeah.

455
39:51.869 --> 39:54.747
I had no work all week and finally hauled one load today.

456
39:57.291 --> 39:58.125
This damn leg.

457
39:59.710 --> 40:02.171
I walked just a little, and it's acting up again.

458
40:02.254 --> 40:05.216
You earned that wound fighting for our country. Look after it.

459
40:08.761 --> 40:10.471
Kkot-nim, eat before it gets cold.

460
40:10.554 --> 40:11.722
So hot!

461
40:11.805 --> 40:13.057
Come on, you silly goose.

462
40:13.599 --> 40:14.642
Blow on it first.

463
40:19.355 --> 40:20.606
You should have some too.

464
40:23.776 --> 40:25.694
I haven't had potatoes in a long time.

465
40:25.778 --> 40:26.904
-Potatoes. -Good grief!

466
40:29.448 --> 40:31.742
When did you get here?

467
40:32.368 --> 40:34.703
My baby is hungry.

468
40:34.787 --> 40:35.913
Just give me one.

469
40:38.832 --> 40:40.084
Hey. Here.

470
40:40.167 --> 40:41.001
Have this.

471
40:45.589 --> 40:50.594
It's hot, sweetie. Mommy will blow on it for you.

472
40:55.307 --> 40:57.810
Nom, nom.

473
40:58.519 --> 40:59.687
Bun-i!

474
41:00.396 --> 41:02.940
If you eat it all up, what about me?

475
41:10.364 --> 41:12.741
Mommy needs to eat to make milk.

476
41:18.872 --> 41:21.083
Right. You need to eat too.

477
41:21.166 --> 41:25.004
Did Mrs. Jo-i's baby really die?

478
41:25.087 --> 41:25.921
Yes.

479
41:27.298 --> 41:30.009
She was starving and had no milk to feed her baby.

480
41:31.260 --> 41:33.053
That baby wrap she was holding

481
41:33.637 --> 41:35.389
looked brand-new, didn't it?

482
41:35.472 --> 41:37.349
I'm sure Ga-kyung gave it to her.

483
41:38.058 --> 41:40.519
Kkot-nim got constipation medicine, No-ma got a bicycle,

484
41:41.020 --> 41:42.938
I got these rubber shoes,

485
41:43.731 --> 41:45.274
and you got some salve.

486
41:45.357 --> 41:46.233
My goodness.

487
41:47.318 --> 41:49.903
She left something for everyone, before moving so far away.

488
41:49.987 --> 41:51.113
What's the point?

489
41:51.780 --> 41:53.657
She left without even saying goodbye.

490
41:55.534 --> 41:57.244
She's gone so far away to America.

491
41:57.870 --> 41:59.580
We may never get to see her again.

492
42:01.624 --> 42:02.750
Ga-kyung

493
42:03.626 --> 42:05.544
will be all right in America, won't she?

494
42:05.628 --> 42:06.503
Of course.

495
42:07.504 --> 42:10.215
She'd find her way out of a tiger's den.

496
42:13.510 --> 42:16.221
I miss Ga-kyung.

497
42:27.983 --> 42:28.984
You're here?

498
42:34.948 --> 42:35.783
I'm sorry.

499
42:37.576 --> 42:38.410
What?

500
42:39.787 --> 42:41.246
I misunderstood earlier.

501
42:41.330 --> 42:43.457
We were at the Inspector General's Office.

502
42:44.416 --> 42:45.376
Is that what you mean?

503
42:46.126 --> 42:47.544
Don't worry about it.

504
42:47.628 --> 42:51.757
I'm used to being the first suspect whenever something goes missing.

505
42:55.469 --> 42:56.303
I'm sorry.

506
42:58.389 --> 42:59.348
Ms. Keum.

507
43:02.017 --> 43:02.893
I trust you.

508
43:04.019 --> 43:05.062
I don't suspect you.

509
43:08.899 --> 43:09.733
Well…

510
43:14.863 --> 43:15.906
Let's go.

511
43:20.411 --> 43:23.789
Today, I'm having the most expensive meal in Gyeongseong.

512
43:23.872 --> 43:25.708
I'm going to clean out your wallet.

513
43:26.208 --> 43:28.585
Haven't you already cleaned out my wallet?

514
43:29.169 --> 43:30.003
What?

515
43:30.629 --> 43:32.756
I have no idea what you're talking about.

516
43:34.133 --> 43:36.343
Please, sir. I can run faster than a bicycle.

517
43:36.427 --> 43:37.886
Gosh, you idiot.

518
43:40.097 --> 43:43.308
Hey, you punk. What kind of delivery boy doesn't have a bicycle?

519
43:46.770 --> 43:48.188
Stay here for a minute.

520
43:49.314 --> 43:50.315
Where are you going?

521
43:50.899 --> 43:51.900
I know him.

522
43:52.484 --> 43:53.318
Sorry?

523
43:53.861 --> 43:54.737
Wait, how…

524
43:55.738 --> 43:57.156
How do you know him?

525
43:57.239 --> 43:59.575
He's the brother of a kid I'm tutoring.

526
43:59.658 --> 44:01.452
Tutoring?

527
44:01.535 --> 44:02.953
But what kind of tutoring?

528
44:03.036 --> 44:03.871
Please, just…

529
44:05.831 --> 44:07.124
I think he's hurt. One moment.

530
44:08.709 --> 44:09.710
Don't go.

531
44:11.920 --> 44:13.797
He'll be embarrassed if you see him like that.

532
44:14.965 --> 44:15.799
What?

533
44:15.883 --> 44:19.219
Have you no shame? Isn't this too much?

534
44:19.303 --> 44:20.929
Whatever, I don't care.

535
44:21.013 --> 44:22.639
Just get out of here.

536
44:22.723 --> 44:24.266
-Sir. -Go away.

537
44:26.977 --> 44:28.020
Come on, let's go.

538
44:32.649 --> 44:33.650
Wait, this won't do.

539
44:33.734 --> 44:35.027
Mr. Sato.

540
44:35.110 --> 44:35.986
Listen.

541
44:36.612 --> 44:39.698
Stay away from those kinds of people. Don't take pity on them.

542
44:40.407 --> 44:41.241
Excuse me?

543
44:41.325 --> 44:44.745
You work for the Government-General, yet you'd help a poor Joseon man?

544
44:44.828 --> 44:47.122
Do you think your father would be happy if he found out?

545
44:47.706 --> 44:48.540
Ms. Keum.

546
44:49.249 --> 44:52.002
He's way beneath you, you know.

547
44:52.753 --> 44:55.339
So keep your distance. Stay away from him.

548
44:55.422 --> 44:57.466
Don't get involved with him again, okay?

549
45:01.637 --> 45:04.348
You sound more like a Government-General official than I do.

550
45:05.474 --> 45:06.308
What?

551
45:06.934 --> 45:07.893
You weren't

552
45:08.560 --> 45:11.355
any different from him before you joined the Government-General.

553
45:11.438 --> 45:12.773
Neither was I.

554
45:12.856 --> 45:15.234
Have you already forgotten those days? He's beneath me?

555
45:16.777 --> 45:18.862
You've adapted perfectly to the Government-General.

556
45:19.530 --> 45:20.781
Well, that figures.

557
45:20.864 --> 45:23.116
I suppose you're clever enough to have caught

558
45:24.368 --> 45:25.536
Mr. Yoo's eye.

559
45:28.247 --> 45:32.209
Well, what do you know about me?

560
45:34.127 --> 45:36.296
And why am I the only one getting the blame?

561
45:36.380 --> 45:39.132
You came from the streets yourself,

562
45:39.216 --> 45:41.718
but you've adapted perfectly as a Japanese now.

563
45:43.470 --> 45:44.763
You know what?

564
45:44.847 --> 45:47.808
An elite from Tokyo Imperial University and the inspector general's son

565
45:47.891 --> 45:49.768
playing teacher to some poor Joseon kid.

566
45:49.852 --> 45:50.978
That's so obnoxious.

567
45:59.111 --> 45:59.945
That's enough.

568
46:04.658 --> 46:05.492
I'm sorry.

569
46:07.578 --> 46:09.079
I just…

570
46:09.955 --> 46:12.457
I just wanted you to be careful.

571
46:12.541 --> 46:13.500
Forget it.

572
46:14.334 --> 46:15.919
Thanks for the reality check.

573
46:16.920 --> 46:18.672
Wait, that's not what I meant.

574
46:18.755 --> 46:19.631
Let's have dinner

575
46:20.757 --> 46:21.592
some other time.

576
46:23.635 --> 46:24.761
I'll see you tomorrow.

577
46:27.556 --> 46:28.640
No, wait.

578
46:34.479 --> 46:36.273
Darn it, this is driving me crazy.

579
46:36.356 --> 46:38.150
How do they know each other?

580
46:41.320 --> 46:44.364
And how did he get his bicycle stolen?

581
46:46.116 --> 46:47.075
It's bugging me.

582
46:51.413 --> 46:53.332
And why does he look so sad,

583
46:53.415 --> 46:55.459
trudging along like a drenched puppy?

584
46:55.542 --> 46:56.877
He's making me feel awful.

585
47:08.430 --> 47:09.306
What?

586
47:10.349 --> 47:11.808
You'll marry Sato Hideo?

587
47:12.601 --> 47:13.435
Yes.

588
47:13.518 --> 47:14.728
Getting married?

589
47:15.437 --> 47:17.356
To a guy like Sato of all people?

590
47:17.439 --> 47:18.982
Do you realize how dangerous that is?

591
47:20.442 --> 47:21.860
Absolutely not.

592
47:22.444 --> 47:25.948
It's not as though I can just say no to this marriage.

593
47:27.741 --> 47:30.702
The wedding will take place once the foreign commission leaves this summer.

594
47:30.786 --> 47:33.830
I don't want to marry him, but if I can't avoid it,

595
47:34.414 --> 47:36.458
I'll try to see what I can do later.

596
47:39.920 --> 47:42.130
Why are we fighting for independence?

597
47:44.758 --> 47:47.094
Why have we all come together?

598
47:48.136 --> 47:51.682
So that we can all live with dignity on our own land.

599
47:51.765 --> 47:53.475
But independence can't come

600
47:53.558 --> 47:56.019
at the cost of destroying your life.

601
47:58.230 --> 47:59.564
-But… -Myung-nam.

602
48:01.191 --> 48:02.484
In the past, we've…

603
48:09.408 --> 48:10.325
Never mind.

604
48:10.909 --> 48:12.119
In the past?

605
48:13.912 --> 48:16.415
What happened in the past?

606
48:21.169 --> 48:23.422
If Sato dies, the marriage will be called off.

607
48:26.675 --> 48:29.136
It was only arranged because he's the inspector general.

608
48:30.053 --> 48:30.887
You mean…

609
48:35.475 --> 48:36.309
Okay.

610
48:36.810 --> 48:39.271
I'll use my position as Sato Hideo's fiancée,

611
48:39.354 --> 48:40.856
and see what I can do for now.

612
48:42.607 --> 48:43.442
Okay.

613
48:45.902 --> 48:46.737
By the way,

614
48:47.446 --> 48:49.531
what happened in the past?

615
48:50.741 --> 48:53.952
Last time, you were telling us something, but you never finished.

616
49:04.421 --> 49:06.089
Years ago, we…

617
49:13.805 --> 49:16.850
I put someone's life in danger.

618
49:20.395 --> 49:23.690
And I put the person she loved through hell.

619
49:28.070 --> 49:28.904
What's that?

620
49:33.033 --> 49:34.618
Sato Hideo brought it.

621
49:34.701 --> 49:36.411
Sato Hideo?

622
49:36.495 --> 49:37.412
Yes.

623
49:37.496 --> 49:39.081
He comes by every so often.

624
49:39.164 --> 49:41.291
He asks me to take good care of Mr. Suzuki

625
49:41.374 --> 49:43.710
since he has no family to visit him.

626
49:44.377 --> 49:47.089
I guess he worries about him since they worked together

627
49:47.172 --> 49:48.256
even if only briefly.

628
49:51.468 --> 49:53.095
It's time for rounds. Let's go.

629
49:53.178 --> 49:54.137
All right.

630
49:55.597 --> 49:57.557
Suzuki?

631
50:00.310 --> 50:02.395
-Suzuki, can you hear me? -Mr. Suzuki.

632
50:05.148 --> 50:07.150
Is my name still

633
50:08.360 --> 50:09.569
Suzuki?

634
50:12.114 --> 50:12.948
Come on.

635
50:14.449 --> 50:17.786
I've been to the other side and back,

636
50:19.329 --> 50:21.581
and we still haven't won our independence?

637
50:52.070 --> 50:52.946
Mr. Sato!

638
51:04.791 --> 51:05.625
I'm sorry.

639
51:08.879 --> 51:10.672
I shouldn't have said that.

640
51:13.884 --> 51:14.718
I'm sorry.

641
51:23.185 --> 51:24.102
I missed

642
51:25.228 --> 51:26.062
the streetcar.

643
51:27.772 --> 51:29.983
I wanted to apologize.

644
51:31.276 --> 51:32.444
Will you accept

645
51:33.278 --> 51:35.572
my apology?

646
51:39.326 --> 51:41.578
I'll buy you a drink.

647
51:42.662 --> 51:43.538
Come with me.

648
51:46.833 --> 51:47.667
Let's go.

649
51:52.130 --> 51:52.964
No.

650
51:56.635 --> 51:57.677
It's my treat.

651
51:58.178 --> 51:59.179
I promised.

652
52:02.557 --> 52:03.725
Except…

653
52:04.517 --> 52:06.895
you didn't say "please."

654
52:06.978 --> 52:07.896
I'm sorry?

655
52:39.803 --> 52:40.720
Thank you.

656
52:43.139 --> 52:44.474
Oh my.

657
52:44.557 --> 52:47.852
Beer really is golden, just like I heard.

658
52:50.272 --> 52:53.316
I was just going to buy him a glass of rice wine.

659
52:53.400 --> 52:55.694
Doesn't he ever take you out to places like this?

660
52:55.777 --> 52:56.611
Sorry?

661
53:00.699 --> 53:03.493
Of course not. He wouldn't bring me somewhere like this.

662
53:03.576 --> 53:06.663
You know, it'd look bad if people saw us.

663
53:07.622 --> 53:08.581
You know how it is.

664
53:17.799 --> 53:19.592
Thanks for the drink.

665
53:44.993 --> 53:47.162
Can I have one more glass?

666
54:12.937 --> 54:14.522
By the way,

667
54:15.315 --> 54:18.234
what's your Joseon name?

668
54:22.655 --> 54:25.075
I was just wondering.

669
54:25.825 --> 54:28.787
You must have had one before.

670
54:33.750 --> 54:35.335
Then let me ask something else.

671
54:35.960 --> 54:38.880
Why did you become an interpreter?

672
54:41.299 --> 54:43.510
Was it money, like it was for me?

673
54:45.303 --> 54:48.723
You can be honest with me. It's nothing to hide.

674
54:53.061 --> 54:55.230
I don't belong anywhere anyway.

675
54:58.733 --> 55:00.151
Even with a gun in my hands,

676
55:02.112 --> 55:04.364
I wouldn't know which way to point it.

677
55:12.580 --> 55:13.415
Why?

678
55:14.207 --> 55:16.376
Are you disappointed that I'm not in it for the money

679
55:16.459 --> 55:17.377
like you are?

680
55:17.460 --> 55:18.586
Yes.

681
55:20.964 --> 55:24.467
I thought you and I had something in common.

682
55:25.969 --> 55:27.470
I guess I was wrong.

683
55:27.554 --> 55:31.015
Someone like you who lives in luxury and a starving nobody like me

684
55:31.099 --> 55:33.143
could never be equals.

685
55:37.021 --> 55:39.232
And what's so terrible about money?

686
55:40.275 --> 55:42.652
At least money doesn't lie.

687
55:42.735 --> 55:45.864
Whether it's Japanese, Joseon, or American money,

688
55:45.947 --> 55:49.492
once it's in your pocket, it buys you food just the same.

689
55:57.167 --> 55:58.042
There was a time

690
56:00.086 --> 56:04.132
when I had no idea where I belonged either.

691
56:06.968 --> 56:08.261
Whenever I felt that way…

692
56:10.513 --> 56:11.681
Mom.

693
56:12.348 --> 56:15.685
I was playing with the other kids today,

694
56:16.519 --> 56:21.441
and some man called us Joseon pigs.

695
56:23.276 --> 56:24.194
He did?

696
56:25.236 --> 56:26.196
Yes.

697
56:26.279 --> 56:33.077
I try not to think about it, but I can't stop thinking about it.

698
56:35.330 --> 56:38.333
When that happens, just keep walking.

699
56:39.042 --> 56:40.668
Keep walking?

700
56:44.297 --> 56:48.551
Because where your feet stand is more real than what's in your mind.

701
56:50.595 --> 56:52.805
The ground beneath your feet

702
56:53.765 --> 56:54.849
is yours,

703
56:56.184 --> 56:57.393
and that's your path.

704
57:01.689 --> 57:04.526
You don't know who your father is, do you?

705
57:05.193 --> 57:07.070
I bet you've got Jap blood in you too.

706
57:11.241 --> 57:12.534
Whenever that happened,

707
57:13.201 --> 57:15.578
I just kept walking.

708
57:17.121 --> 57:18.831
Because where my feet stand

709
57:19.374 --> 57:22.252
is more real than what's in my mind.

710
57:28.758 --> 57:32.136
So I kept walking and walking.

711
57:33.471 --> 57:36.057
But there was no path and nothing in sight.

712
57:38.518 --> 57:39.519
Then…

713
58:23.187 --> 58:25.815
just when I really felt like giving up…

714
59:20.953 --> 59:23.373
I finally saw the path.

715
59:24.749 --> 59:26.292
What was it?

716
59:27.418 --> 59:29.045
Going to America.

717
59:31.005 --> 59:33.800
There is the tallest building in the world.

718
59:33.883 --> 59:36.260
They said I could climb all the way to the top.

719
59:36.344 --> 59:38.554
So I made up my mind to go there.

720
59:40.223 --> 59:43.142
I'm going to make it to America.

721
59:43.768 --> 59:46.104
I'll save enough money to go to America

722
59:46.187 --> 59:48.856
and climb all the way to the top of the building.

723
59:52.318 --> 59:53.403
And then what?

724
59:54.320 --> 59:55.279
What?

725
01:00:00.743 --> 01:00:01.911
Once you get up there,

726
01:00:02.995 --> 01:00:04.122
what will you do next?

727
01:00:04.914 --> 01:00:05.873
Well…

728
01:00:09.752 --> 01:00:10.795
I don't know.

729
01:00:11.921 --> 01:00:14.590
I guess I'll find out when I get there.

730
01:00:15.216 --> 01:00:18.553
You won't know where a path leads until you take it.

731
01:00:22.432 --> 01:00:23.808
So,

732
01:00:24.434 --> 01:00:25.768
you should

733
01:00:27.103 --> 01:00:29.689
take one step forward.

734
01:00:30.857 --> 01:00:32.358
Who knows?

735
01:00:33.192 --> 01:00:35.737
You might discover what you really want.

736
01:00:39.198 --> 01:00:40.366
Never mind.

737
01:00:40.992 --> 01:00:43.786
Oh, come on.

738
01:00:45.163 --> 01:00:47.248
Now, just do as I say.

739
01:00:47.331 --> 01:00:50.877
First, close your eyes and count to three.

740
01:00:50.960 --> 01:00:52.628
Then open them,

741
01:00:52.712 --> 01:00:55.715
and whatever you see first, make that your goal.

742
01:00:56.758 --> 01:00:58.134
You should try it sometime.

743
01:00:58.217 --> 01:01:01.429
You have to pay for everything except breathing in this world.

744
01:01:01.512 --> 01:01:04.223
This is one thing you can do for free. You just need to blink.

745
01:01:34.128 --> 01:01:37.298
I'm not making it up. It's true.

746
01:01:40.635 --> 01:01:41.469
Yes.

747
01:01:44.096 --> 01:01:45.264
I suppose you're right.

748
01:01:47.767 --> 01:01:49.519
What?

749
01:01:50.353 --> 01:01:52.104
I can't hear you with all this noise.

750
01:02:01.739 --> 01:02:02.824
It's Kim Tae-ung.

751
01:02:05.785 --> 01:02:06.953
My Joseon name.

752
01:02:59.171 --> 01:03:03.092
100 DAYS OF DECEPTION

753
01:03:03.175 --> 01:03:06.637
She might've told Sato Hideo things she shouldn't have while drunk.

754
01:03:06.721 --> 01:03:08.347
I don't understand…

755
01:03:10.600 --> 01:03:11.726
Mr. Sato!

756
01:03:11.809 --> 01:03:15.813
I think Sato Hideo has feelings for Seo-hee.

757
01:03:15.897 --> 01:03:19.525
There'll be several senior officials from the Government-General that day.

758
01:03:19.609 --> 01:03:22.695
We can't afford to miss this opportunity.

759
01:03:22.778 --> 01:03:24.864
You'll set off a bomb at the banquet?

760
01:03:26.282 --> 01:03:28.826
No. You'll never get a bomb inside.

761
01:03:31.829 --> 01:03:34.206
So in the end, you chose to do something stupid.

762
01:03:40.421 --> 01:03:42.423
Subtitle translation by: Youji Kim
